From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:20:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] download: pick the download quality separately from playback

Episodes queued without a chosen video used to take the source's
playback preference (preferred / sortVideos), so downloads were as
small as what was streamed. Add Settings -> Downloads -> "Download
quality" (harmony_download_quality): Highest available (default),
Up to 2160p/1440p/1080p/720p/480p/360p, or Same as playback.

DownloadQualitySelector loads every non-lazy hoster, ranks videos by
height (Video.resolution or "1080p" / "1920x1080" / "4K" in the title;
tallest not above the cap, then shortest above it, then videos without
a height by label: High > auto > plain > Low, reversed for caps <= 480p)
and resolves them in that order. If nothing resolves, or "Same as
playback" is chosen, the old HosterLoader.getBestVideo path is used.
A quality picked in the per-episode dialog still wins.

Anikku only: Mihon has no video quality; Animeko's single resource
preference already ranks 2160p > 1440p > 1080p > 720p for playback and
caching, and manual caching lets the user pick the exact resource.
